tion is still very  tense and we have been keeping alert and  this is the situation that we say china  is trying to destroy the status quo or  at least the symbol of the sales quote  which is the median line of the taiwan  strait you know the medium line of  taiwan strait has been there for decades  safeguarding peace and stability over  the taiwan strait and without that  tested agreement the two militaries are  going to come very close to each other  and the chinese are coming so close that  it  compressed the depths of our air defense  and it can create a very dangerous  situation uh status quo across the  taiwan strait has been uh been seen as  the interest of all parties concerned in  this area or  globally and when china is trying to  destroy the status quo is not in the  interest of us  or the international community minister  you talked about the median lie but  china says they have never agreed on  that does that mean this unofficial  demarcation line is not there anymore uh  we wish that or i should say yeah we  hope that it's still there because it's  been there for decades safeguarding  peace and stability across the taiwan  strait uh the chinese uh has this long  plane  in destroying the cisco  uh their military spokesperson last year  uh last june uh say that there's no such  thing as the medium line of the town  straight  uh and this year uh the spokesperson of  the ministry of foreign affairs say that  the whole taiwan strait is china's  waters  it's not international water it belongs  china's sovereignty and china has a  sovereign jurisdiction over the taiwan  strait but taiwan strait in reality has  been international water for a long long  time and therefore the chinese have this  point  to make sure  that its claims  can support  its military activities and this is  exactly what they are trying to do they  say there's no such thing as the medium  line of the town straight and they fly  their airplanes across the medium line  and these kinds of activities are  destabilizing  and it's provocative and can be very  dangerous and we oppose it uh and i  think the international community  especially coming from the federal  democracies they all oppose what china  has been doing  now you've described the the exercises  that have been taking place and you  describe this kind of ratchet effect  of great attention across the strait but  you describe the exercise as a kind of  rehearsal uh for for a potential  invasion  um  what is your sense are you concerned  that an invasion really is potentially  coming and if so what kind of a timeline  are you currently looking at well i  cannot comment on the timeline  but if you look at the chinese statement  the statements coming from their senior  officials  they've been saying that taiwan belongs  to china  and they want to unify with taiwan  peacefully if possible and by force if  necessary and this is not only some  officials it's virtually all officials  are talking about this beginning from xi  jinping himself  and in order to substantiate this kind  of claim  they have been conducting military  exercises along the taiwan strait or  around taiwan for a long time  if you look at the trajectory of their  military threat against taiwan  in the last few years you see more and  more chinese airplanes there are sorties  coming close to our adiz  and they are flying closer and closer to  taiwan  and their ships are also increasing in  number  creating threat scenarios  so if you put all this together you see  that the chinese seems to be preparing  for a war against taiwan for what they  claim unification  of their country so  what they were doing at the first part  of august uh  which is a  exercise according to their playbook  against taiwan uh let me say it again  they fired missiles to the waters near  taiwan  they conducted very large scale air and  sea exercises they conducted cyber  attacks against taiwan they conducted a  disinformation campaign against taiwan  and at t