vernment was imposing the  national security law on hong kong to  take away every bit of freedom away from  the hong kong people  a lot of people around the world are  asking  is chinese government going to stop at  hong kong or who is the next and at that  time a lot of people are already talking  about taiwan might be the next and i  think the story can go further  is taiwan going to be the last target  of the chinese authoritarian expansion  i would say no  the reason is very clear china also  claims east china sea and they'll be  conducting military exercises or sending  their ships to the disputed water china  also claims south china sea and their  daily patrol of the south china sea  either by their bombers or by their  warships uh is uh so frequent uh these  days is china limited uh what is the  chinese ambition limited to east china  sea taiwan strait and the south china  sea i can tell you no if it's not  stopped  china already signed a security  agreement with the sonoma islands which  is very far away from china  and if we don't stop it  the chinese government is going to sign  more security agreements with more  pacific countries  remember  the chinese leader has already said the  pacific ocean is big enough to  accommodate china and the united states  that's how ambitious they are and are  they limited to the indo-pacific region  or the pacific area i would say no if  you look at the naval bases they are  building in the  cambodia  in myanmar  in pakistan  in sri lanka all the way to djibouti i  think they have global ambition  and the expansion of authoritarianism  always is at the cost of democracy and i  think it's a time for democracy to unite  to stop the authoritarianism from  expanding further mr wu though um i mean  how seriously is taiwan taking this  threat in military terms i mean  we've heard very recently taiwan is  increasing its defense budget by almost  14 from 2022 to 2023 but that still just  takes defense spending to 2.4 percent of  g