ndle these days um  maybe all of a sudden the chinese people  will say that uh no this is not what we  want we want something like taiwan so  you counting on the the chinese  communist party collapsing and democracy  coming to china is that your greatest  hope  no that's not what i say and i'm not  going to predict  but we have faith in taiwan's democracy  as long as we are democratic i think we  will be doing fine the chinese military  threat is there that is one fact that we  have to reckon with and will continue to  beef up our defense capabilities  so that we can defend ourselves but at  the same time the chinese military  threat is there and if the chinese  military threat against taiwan is  unwelcome not only by the taiwanese  people but also by  the world at large i think the  international community will come  together and tell the chinese leaders  that you are military trade against  taiwan is not a good solution  minister um now we come to the name of  taiwan well we say taiwan all the time  in english but we all know that in  taiwan the constitution that you abide  by is the constitution of republic china  so we when we talk about this confusion  is your government um pursuing the jury  independence is this a long-term dream  uh that's a very good question  the president president tai was elected  based upon the promises to the people  that we would safeguard the status quo  uh we would look at the status quo as  serving the best interest of all parties  concerned and therefore the policy of  this government is to safely safeguard  the status quo the status quo  that the republic of china taiwan and  the people's republic of china have no  jurisdiction over each other the status  quo that taiwan is already a democracy  the status quo that taiwanese people  have a say over taiwan's future so this  is a status quo over taiwan and that's a  policy that we are pursuing yet you are  on the china's list of taiwan  independence die hards  that's what they claim 